       :before
       "Rule source/facts and applicability visible? Unsafe fixes rejected? Baseline/fail-on-new reproducible? [Linter](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/180-t4-linter-specification.md) Require rule id/severity/inputs/fixability/profile/target and source/manifest spans; cover every T4 rule class, JSON/SARIF, baseline and rule-coverage artifacts, stable explain-rule output and combined source/manifest analysis. Reject unknown rules, unavailable facts, policy-forbidden stale spans, unchecked fixes and policy-blocking release findings. Foundation requirement gravity/canonical-concept-vocabulary: Publish the D3 reference meanings and relationships for profile, target, backend, runtime, effect, capability, safety outcome, artifact and file, and check representative compiler/package/runtime manifests against those meanings. Refusals: Reject a manifest that equates an effect with authority, a profile with a backend, or an artifact with its storage file; retain the offending span/field and owning concept reference. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Foundation requirement gravity/cross-phase-term-change-control: Before downstream reliance on a changed cross-phase concept, update the canonical D3 definition and affected contract/schema references together, record the compatibility decision and invalidate dependent terminology checks. Refusals: Reject use of a changed downstream meaning with an unchanged canonical definition, stale dependent checks or an unrecorded compatibility impact. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-each-claimed-component-to-exact-implementation-and-conformance - Exact component/slice contracts, declared unsupported scope and claimed-support evidence. Foundation requirement gravity/domain-concept-layer-map: Publish a domain-concept map relating each declared concept to its source forms, Core/domain IR boundary, emitted artifact, effects and required capabilities; verify a representative domain product against that map. Refusals: Reject an unmapped claimed concept, a host API substituted for its source meaning or a mapping that treats an effect declaration as a capability grant. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Foundation requirement gravity/qualify-ambiguous-normative-terms: For normative uses whose meaning affects implementation, require an explicit qualified D3 concept or owning contract reference; report the exact ambiguous span and the competing interpretations. Refusals: Reject unqualified uses such as runtime/profile/target or effect/capability where they change the required implementation meaning; ordinary nonnormative prose does not create a new terminology gate. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion."}],
