       :raw-sha256
       "800d05e67679c2d3a33fef7c5206e3bed14e1651925b4af02d3847692bad2f21",
       :raw
       "- Dynamic eval is rejected for firmware, kernel, hardware, no-runtime, and\n  package policies that deny it.\n",
       :source-occurrence-id
       "R9/source/b8b06e97f376a566ec3820ffc9cc22d23e7ffeb26be81d2f24a24656f2f93cad",
       :id "facet/runtime-domains-schema/r9/000e7ac4d0f3c217a053ed50",
       :kind :condition,
       :document-id "R9",
       :end-byte 1568,
       :start-byte 1460}
      {:path
       "docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/120-r9-repl-and-interactive-runtime-design.md",
       :raw-sha256
       "bbcf8b7ce61a61f22eb4c6d173b95ad9c1a849aedcc6efb4ee51fe2d6918be29",
       :raw
       "Interactive forms pass through the same reader, macro expansion, name\nresolution, type checking, effect checking, capability checking, safety\nanalysis, profile validation, lowering, and runtime selection as file-based\ncode. The REPL may expose intermediate snapshots, but it may not skip checks for\nsafe execution.\n",
       :source-occurrence-id
       "R9/source/1929e3f0715fd2b6e86cbe63c5e0e9c9c5735c3f47ee8700435e86db18554656",
       :id "facet/runtime-domains-schema/r9/03d5b80f8e45977ce6fcca71",
       :kind :condition,
       :document-id "R9",
       :end-byte 3735,
       :start-byte 3420}
